// Standard Capability Interface: Actions
//
// Hosts implement this interface to do one thing in a connected app for a
// program, without an agent run and without putting any app names or business
// verbs into the host interface. Application libraries (`X`, `Gmail`, …) are
// written in Norn on top of it.
//
// An action is done in two requests of the host (spec §6.3):
//   prepare  fixes exactly what will be done and has the host admit it, as its
//            policy for that app requires; nothing is done yet
//   perform  does what was prepared, once

// An action of a connected app. `'i` is what it takes, `'o` what it answers.
type action<'i, 'o>

// An admitted action with its input fixed. Only `prepare` answers one.
type prepared<'o>

// The action `name` of the connected app `app`, as in action("x", "post").
// The checker reads both type arguments against the app's connector manifest.
external action: (string, string) => action<'i, 'o>

// Fixes `input` and asks the host to admit the action.
//   Answered(prepared)  admitted: it can be performed
//   Refused(why)        the host's policy, or whoever it asked, declined
//   Broke(why)          it cannot be prepared: bad input, app not connected
external prepare: (action<'i, 'o>, 'i, ~by: 'd=?, ~about: 'c=?) => request<prepared<'o>>

// Does what was prepared, once.
//   Answered(result)    done
//   Refused(why)        the admission no longer holds, or it was performed before
//   Broke(why)          it failed, or its outcome is unknown; the host does not try again
external perform: (prepared<'o>, ~by: 'd=?) => request<'o>
